# Gnome world's vocabulary, which the module sees #
# The world: 896 tiles across and 208 down, row 0 the top of the sky; the page holds its tiles. A kind of ground: 0 air, 1 soil, 2 clay, 3 sand and gravel, 4 sandstone, 5 shale, 6 limestone, 7 granite, 8 the gnomes' stone masonry, 9 their timber. Dug and porous: soil, sand and gravel, sandstone; dug, not porous: clay, shale; not dug, porous: limestone; not dug, not porous: granite #
# A ground's nature: its kind, its name, the steps a gnome takes to dig a tile of it (0 when it cannot be dug), the share of it that is pores, which water can fill (hundredths), how fast water moves through it (thousandths of its pores a step), the share of its pores water clings to after the rest drains (hundredths), and its color (0xRRGGBB) #
type Ground = (kind = Int, name = String, dig = Int, pores = Int, flow = Int, cling = Int, color = Int) in
# A layer under the ground: its kind, and how thick it is at every 16th column (57 of them), in tiles; the layers lie one under another from the surface down #
type Layer = (kind = Int, thick = [Int]) in
# A place in the world: its kind, where it is (x, y: a tile), its size (w, h) and a number to vary it by. Kinds: 10 a creek, 11 a stream, 12 a river (x its left edge, y the water's top row, w the water's width, h its depth); 13 a beaver lodge (x, w), 14 a beaver dam (x, w: across its river; v the logs it starts with); 15 a beaver (x its lodge, w its dam, v which); 20 the gnomes' village (x, y its top-left, w, h); 21 a hamlet, a smaller one; 30 a great tree with ladders, 31 a great tree with a stair inside its trunk (x the trunk's middle, y its foot, h its height, v its seed); 40 a bowl of clay holding water (x, y its top-left, w, h); 41 a bed of old river gravel; 42 a shelf of limestone with caves; 43 a body of granite; 44 a vein of gems (v how many); 45 a boulder; 50 a tree (v its kind: 0 an oak, 1 a pine, 2 a birch, 3 an aspen, 4 a willow; h its height); 51 a bush; 52 a spring; 53 a mushroom (v: 0 red-capped, 1 brown); 54 flowers (v: 0 daisies, 1 poppies, 2 bluebells, 3 buttercups, 4 lupines; h how many, one to three) #
type Place = (kind = Int, x = Int, y = Int, w = Int, h = Int, v = Int) in
# A batch of places by chance: their kind, how many, and for each of x, y, w, h and v the least and the spread above it #
type Spec = (kind = Int, n = Int, x0 = Int, xr = Int, y0 = Int, yr = Int, w0 = Int, wr = Int, h0 = Int, hr = Int, v0 = Int, vr = Int) in
# A world's plan: its seed; the surface's row at every 8th column (113 of them); the layers, top down; the water table's row at every 16th column; the places #
type Plan = (seed = Int, surface = [Int], layers = [Layer], table = [Int], places = [Place]) in
# A room of a village, deep underground: its kind (0 the hall, 1 a kitchen, 2 a bedroom, 3 a pantry, 4 a workshop, 5 a library, 6 a dining room, 7 a bath house, 8 a mushroom cellar, 9 a well room, 10 a sitting room, 11 a weaving room, 12 a nursery), where it is (x, y its top-left inside, w, h, in tiles), and what goes up from it to the surface: 0 nothing, 1 a light shaft, 2 an air shaft, 3 a chimney #
type Room = (kind = Int, x = Int, y = Int, w = Int, h = Int, up = Int) in
# A thing in a room (the page draws each kind): its kind, where it stands across the room (tenths of a tile from the room's left) and its width (tenths of a tile) #
type Thing = (kind = Int, at = Int, w = Int) in
# A great tree's limb: the row it leaves the trunk at (counted up from the tree's foot), its side (-1 left, 1 right), its length in tiles, the house on its end (-1 none; 0 to 15 a style of tree house; 100 a bird house, 101 a squirrel's house) and whether a rope bridge goes from it across to the next limb up #
type Limb = (y = Int, side = Int, len = Int, house = Int, bridge = Bool) in
# A tree house's style, gnome-made, craftsman: its name, its Latin name, its roof (0 a low gable, 1 a steep gable, 2 a hip, 3 a mushroom cap, 4 an acorn cap, 5 a cone, 6 a dome, 7 a shed roof, 8 thatch), its walls' color, its roof's, its trim's (0xRRGGBB), how its walls are made (0 shingles, 1 boards and battens, 2 logs, 3 half-timbering, 4 stone below and shingles above, 5 stone, 6 birch bark, 7 plaster), its windows (0 square, 1 round, 2 diamond panes, 3 arched), and one thing more (0 none, 1 a porch on tapered posts, 2 a balcony, 3 a turret, 4 a chimney, 5 a dormer, 6 a bell, 7 a telescope, 8 a flower box, 9 a rain barrel, 10 a weathervane, 11 a beehive) #
type Style = (name = String, latin = String, roof = Int, walls = Int, roofc = Int, trim = Int, clad = Int, win = Int, more = Int) in
# A beaver: where it is (x, in hundredths of a tile), the way it faces (-1, 1), its job (0 resting in its lodge, 1 going to a tree, 2 gnawing it, 3 dragging a log to the dam, 4 laying it, 5 going home, 6 going back to its pile of logs, 7 cutting a log from a fallen tree), the steps left at it, its tree, or its pile of logs (x, -1 none), its lodge's x and its dam's x; and what it did this step: felled its tree (its x, -1 none), laid a log on the dam (true), cut a log from the fallen tree onto its pile (true) #
type Beaver = (x = Int, face = Int, job = Int, t = Int, tree = Int, lodge = Int, dam = Int, felled = Int, laid = Bool, cut = Bool) in
# ---- The gnome, a step at a time (sixty a second) ---- #
# The gnome: where its feet are (x their middle, y their bottom, in thousandths of a tile), its speed (thousandths of a tile a step), the way it faces (-1, 1), whether it stands on something, climbs, floats at the water's surface or is under it, its breath (steps of it left, 600 at most), whether it has the diving gear, its digger (0 none, 1 the good digger, 2 the super digger), the tile it is digging (column dc, row dr; -1 none) and the steps it has dug it, and what happened this step: 0 nothing, 1 a tile dug out (dc, dr), 2 a jump, 3 into the water, 4 out of breath, 5 a dive #
type Gnome = (x = Int, y = Int, vx = Int, vy = Int, face = Int, ground = Bool, climb = Bool, swim = Bool, under = Bool, air = Int, gear = Bool, tool = Int, dc = Int, dr = Int, dt = Int, ev = Int) in
# What the gnome feels round it: the tiles in a window three across (columns cx - 1 to cx + 1) and five down (rows cy - 3 to cy + 1), cx and cy the tile its feet stand in; each row one number, its three tiles 128 apart (the left one the least). A tile's number: what is there (0 open, 1 to 7 a kind of ground, 8 masonry, 9 timber, 10 a boulder, 11 a platform, open from below), and 16 more where water fills it, 32 more where the gnome can climb (a ladder, the stair, a tunnel dug) #
type Near = (cx = Int, cy = Int, r0 = Int, r1 = Int, r2 = Int, r3 = Int, r4 = Int) in
# The keys held: the way across (-1, 0, 1), up, down, and whether up was pressed just now (a jump) #
type Pad = (dx = Int, up = Bool, down = Bool, jump = Bool, dig = Bool) in
# The gnome as it has moved, halfway through its step (World.step, then World.finish): where it is, its speeds, the column of the wall it ran into (-1 none), whether it stands, climbs, floats, and jumped #
type Moved = (x = Int, y = Int, vx = Int, vy = Int, hc = Int, ground = Bool, climb = Bool, floating = Bool, jumped = Bool) in
# What a villager says: its name, and its line #
type Talk = (name = String, line = String) in
# ---- Roots and mycelium (as Gnome dig's scene grows them, dig/rules/Scene.hz) ---- #
# A line of a root or a thread of mycelium: from x0, y0 to x1, y1, and its width, all in hundredths of a tile (x across the whole world, y down from the top of the sky) #
type Line = (x0 = Int, y0 = Int, x1 = Int, y1 = Int, w = Int) in
